TIP:  The intro and instrumental bridge emulates the banjo part that appears in the recording.  

TIP:  In the 2nd and 4th lines of the verse Darius sings note <b> (e.g. "lot to" and "made me" etc.) and not <c> so (Cmaj7) is the appropriate chord.  But rather than play a regular (Cmaj7) add your pinky to the bass string (top string/3rd fret) and play a (Cmaj7G) including the top string on the strum.

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and add the 5th note as necessary.

   
